adjudication.rationale:
In `packages/core/EventManager.ts`, the diff changes logic to treat `destinationCalendar` as an array:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

When `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null`, `undefined`, or an empty array, `mainHostDestinationCalendar` becomes `undefined`. Accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will then throw a `TypeError` if the left side of the `&&` is true (i.e., when `evt.location === MeetLocationType`). The code lacks optional chaining (`mainHostDestinationCalendar?.integration`) or a guard, so this is a real crash introduced/visible in the diff.
